Gitleaks (rules and key shapes)
================================================================================

Source:   https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks
Version:  v8.30.1
Commit:   83d9cd684c87d95d656c1458ef04895a7f1cbd8e
License:  MIT

Where it is used:
  - third_party/gitleaks/LICENSE: an exact copy of the upstream file at the commit
    above.
  - third_party/gitleaks/gitleaks.toml: a copy of the upstream file at the commit
    above, with one change: the allowlist of the gcp-api-key rule is removed,
    because its 16 entries are whole key-shaped strings. The upstream file has
    SHA-256 e163e53b9e7e8a8511e77271e2b323ed057759542a6d988258afe3a1fa329caf.
  - src/checker/rules.generated.ts: generated from that file by
    `npm run rules:build` (patterns converted and, for a few rules, rewritten).
  - plugin/hooks/lib/checker/rules.generated.ts: a byte-for-byte copy of the
    file above, shipped in the plugin. This file ships beside it.
  - plugin/backup/checker/rules.generated.js: the same rules compiled to JavaScript
    by `npm run plugin:build`, shipped in the plugin for the backup lock. This file
    ships beside it, and in the folder `/redact backup` copies.
  - tools/test-sets/whole-keys.ts and the key shapes in tests/fakes.test.ts:
    written by hand after reading the upstream patterns; some match them exactly.

